\f0 \b \fs28 \pard \s11 \li1209 \fi-1007 \ri1007 \ql Class Methods\
\fs14\
\pard \s42 \li1512 \fi-503 \ri1007 \ql \tx1512 \fs28 \f5 \b0 \fs52 p\tab \f0 \b \fs28 isContextHelpModeActive\
\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 +\'80(BOOL)\b isContextHelpModeActive\b0  \
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Returns YES if the application is currently in context-sensitive help mode, NO otherwise. In context-sensitive help mode, when a user clicks a user interface item, help for that item is displayed in a small window just below the cursor.\
\fs14\
\pard \s57 \li2804 \fi-1292 \ri1007 \ql \tx2799 \tx3282 \tx3771 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 See also:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 +\b \'80setContextHelpModeActive: \
\fs14\
\fs46\
\f0 \fs28 \pard \s43 \li1512 \fi-503 \ri1007 \ql \tx1512 \tx8265 \f5 \b0 \fs52 p\tab \f0 \b \fs28 setContextHelpModeActive:\
\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 +\'80(void)\b setContextHelpModeActive:\b0 (BOOL)\i flag\i0  \
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Controls context-sensitive help mode. If \i flag\i0  is YES, the application enters context-sensitive help mode. If \i flag\i0  is NO, the application returns to normal operation. \
\fs14\
\fs28 You never send this message directly; instead, the NSApplication method \b activateContextHelpMode\b0  activates context-sensitive help mode, and the first mouse click after displaying the context-sensitive help window deactivates it. \
\fs14\
\fs28 When the application enters context-sensitive help mode, NSHelpManager posts NSContextHelpModeDidActivateNotification to the default notification center. When the application returns to normal operation, NSHelpManager posts NSContextHelpModeDidDeactivateNotification. \
\fs14\
\pard \s57 \li2804 \fi-1292 \ri1007 \ql \tx2799 \tx3282 \tx3771 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 See also:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 +\'80\b isContextHelpModeActive\b0  \
\fs14\
\fs46\
\f0 \b \fs28 \pard \s43 \li1512 \fi-503 \ri1007 \ql \tx1512 \tx8265 \f5 \b0 \fs52 p\tab \f0 \b \fs28 sharedHelpManager\
\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 +\'80(NSHelpManager *)\b sharedHelpManager\b0  \
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Returns the shared NSHelpManager instance, creating it if it does not already exist.\
\fs14\
\fs56\
\f0 \b \fs28 \pard \s32 \li1209 \fi-1007 \ri1007 \ql Instance Methods\
\fs14\
\pard \s42 \li1512 \fi-503 \ri1007 \ql \tx1512 \fs28 \f5 \b0 \fs52 p\tab \f0 \b \fs28 contextHelpForObject:\
\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80(NSAttributedString\'80*)\b contextHelpForObject:\b0 (id)\i object\i0  \
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Returns context-sensitive help for \i object\i0 . \
\fs14\
\pard \s57 \li2804 \fi-1292 \ri1007 \ql \tx2799 \tx3282 \tx3771 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 See also:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80\b setContextHelp:forObject:\b0 , \f3 -\f1 \'80\b showContextHelpForObject:locationHint: \
\fs14\
\fs46\
\f0 \fs28 \pard \s43 \li1512 \fi-503 \ri1007 \ql \tx1512 \tx8265 \f5 \b0 \fs52 p\tab \f0 \b \fs28 removeContextHelpForObject:\
\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80(void)\b removeContextHelpForObject:\b0 (id)\i object\i0  \
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Removes the association between \i object\i0  and its context-sensitive help. If object does not have context-sensitive help associated with it, this method does nothing. Typically, you use Interface Builder to remove context-sensitive help from an item.\
\fs14\
\pard \s57 \li2804 \fi-1292 \ri1007 \ql \tx2799 \tx3282 \tx3771 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 See also:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80\b setContextHelp:forObject:\b0  \
\fs14\
\fs46\
\f0 \b \fs28 \pard \s43 \li1512 \fi-503 \ri1007 \ql \tx1512 \tx8265 \f5 \b0 \fs52 p\tab \f0 \b \fs28 setContextHelp:forObject:\
\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80(void)\b setContextHelp:\b0 (NSAttributedString\'80*)\i help\i0  \b forObject:\b0 (id)\i object\i0  \
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Associates \i help\i0  with \i object\i0 . When the application enters context-sensitive help mode, if \i object\i0  is clicked, \i help\i0  will appear in the context-sensitive help window. Typically, you use Interface Builder to associate context-sensitive help with an object. \
\fs14\
\pard \s57 \li2804 \fi-1292 \ri1007 \ql \tx2799 \tx3282 \tx3771 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 See also:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80\b removeContextHelpForObject\b0 : \
\fs14\
\fs46\
\f0 \b \fs28 \pard \s43 \li1512 \fi-503 \ri1007 \ql \tx1512 \tx8265 \f5 \b0 \fs52 p\tab \f0 \b \fs28 showContextHelpForObject:locationHint: \
\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80(BOOL)\b showContextHelpForObject:\b0 (id)\i object\i0  \b locationHint:\b0 (NSPoint)\i point\i0  \
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Displays the context-sensitive help for \i object\i0  at or near the point on the screen specified by \i point\i0 . This point is usually just under the cursor. Returns YES if it successfully displays context-sensitive help for the object, NO if it cannot (for example, if there is no context-sensitive help associated with this object). \
\fs14\
\pard \s57 \li2804 \fi-1292 \ri1007 \ql \tx2799 \tx3282 \tx3771 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 See also:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80\b contextHelpForObject:\b0  \
